WEBVTT

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:10.730
Hello?

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:12.930
We have Sumiyoshi Chisato.

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:14.010
Huh?

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:16.700
If you want her returned to you unharmed, do as I say.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:18.140
Who the hell is this?!

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:19.540
Where's Chisato?

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:24.580
Come to the phone booth in front of the Takafuji school gate at 7 A.M. sharp.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:25.170
What?

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:29.800
I'm not responsible for what happens to the girl if you fail to comply.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:30.720
Understood?

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:33.200
Hey, hold on!

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.960
Dammit. What the hell is...

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:37.100
I have thirty minutes.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.260
That's barely enough time.

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:30.000
Damn it! There's no one here!

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:37.120
Hello?

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:42.340
Now come to the phone booth by the Seaside Park entrance by 7:30 A.M. sharp.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:44.810
Who is this? What do you want?!

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:47.620
Just keep your mouth shut and do as I say.

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:50.310
We'll return the girl eventually.

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:53.360
Also, don't speak to anyone about what happened today.

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:54.790
Not even after the election is over.

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:56.820
Otherwise, you'll regret it.

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:58.900
What are you planning to—

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:00.320
Hey, wait! Hello?

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:00.730
Hatsushiba General Hospital Emergency Entrance

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:01.760
Hello?!

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:02.570
Hatsushiba General Hospital Emergency Entrance

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:05.180
Kana-chan?

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:08.580
Good morning, Michiru.

00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:10.690
Looks like you're awake.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:11.830
Yakumo!

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:15.060
What about the operation?

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:18.220
Don't worry about your job right now.

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:20.060
I remember...

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:23.090
taking pictures of a backroom deal.

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:25.800
Your camera was found broken after the accident.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:27.850
The memory card was missing as well.

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:29.340
I see.

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:30.680
Oh, I almost forgot.

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:33.270
Coming in!

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:36.560
I knew you'd be here, Yakumo-senpai.

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:37.740
Oosawa-kun!

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:39.820
It's Election Day!

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:42.740
The Student Council President,
of all people, can't be late for that!

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:44.030
You have a point.

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:46.620
Please focus on your job.

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:48.790
We'll be here to look after Kana-chan.

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:51.540
V-Very well. Excuse me, then.

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:54.210
Damn it!

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:56.820
Where the hell is Yuu-kun?

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:58.840
Maybe he overslept.

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:04.640
Bad news!

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:07.080
Can you open the ASP homepage?

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.740
Huh? Okay.

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:11.230
What is this?!

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:14.360
It looks like... an exposé article on Yuuki-senpai.

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:15.680
This is nonsense.

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:16.480
This is terrible!

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:19.960
Did you approach us to write this article?

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:20.780
Of course not!

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:23.030
I'll go speak to the club president.

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:34.600
Yuu-kun, where are you right now?

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:35.460
Mii-chan?

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:37.600
An awful rumor is being spread online.

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:38.960
You have to get here now!

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:41.080
Can you hear me, Yuu-kun?

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:42.660
Sorry, Mii-chan.

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:48.740
Damn it!

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:02.620
Damn it!

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:08.860
Hello?

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:11.950
You didn't tell her too much. Very good.

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:13.580
You've got me wiretapped?!

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:15.330
Look under the telephone.

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:20.440
This is Chisato's...

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:24.090
Get the picture? Don't try anything stupid.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:25.160
You...

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:26.340
Next location.

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:30.560
I can't get through. I think he turned off his phone.

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:31.930
I can't get through to Chisato, either.

00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:34.140
Call Yakkun!

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:38.620
Things are looking bad. The drawing to decide the speech order will begin soon.

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:40.270
I'll go in his place!

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:47.240
Sorry for leaving you alone.

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:51.910
I hear you suddenly took Kana-chan out of the hospital.

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:53.360
You can trust us, you know.

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:57.060
We may be an opposing faction, but we're still a part of the Public Safety Commission.

00:05:57.060 --> 00:06:00.440
We'd never put Kana-chan in harm's way!

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:03.590
In any case, it's just wonderful that Kana-chan finally woke up.

00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:05.360
Don't you think it's miraculous?

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:10.720
She was unconscious for over six months and woke up from the sound of a harmonica.

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:12.460
Oh, right!

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:16.580
Is it true that Public Safety was wheeling and dealing with General Affairs?

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:17.500
Yes.

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:18.960
Do you remember who, exactly?

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:21.020
Not at all, actually.

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:22.400
Yeah, I bet.

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:24.610
That's unfortunate.

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:28.220
If only there were some photos available to prove it.

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:29.820
There <i>are</i> photos.

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:30.780
Huh?

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:32.530
There are?

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:35.500
Hey, where can I find those photos?

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:36.450
Will you tell me?

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:39.170
Sure. They're actually...

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:41.130
Black.

00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:44.120
Actually what?

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:48.060
I mean, they were actually saved on the memory card,

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:49.220
but it seems like that was taken.

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:52.350
Oh, I already heard about that.

00:06:52.730 --> 00:06:55.850
I thought I was making progress here. What a shame.

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:59.340
Oh, no. Look how late it is.

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:02.080
Sorry, but I have important business to attend to.

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:03.610
I'll be going back now.

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:06.030
Take care.

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:09.410
Where's Oojima-kun?!

00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:12.480
He's not here yet. We don't know where Chisato is, either.

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:13.900
What's going on?

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:15.910
The order for the speeches has been decided!

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:17.440
What place did we get?

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:18.700
He'll be speaking last!

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:20.000
Great job!

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:21.380
That bought us some time!

00:07:21.380 --> 00:07:23.960
I'm good at drawing lots.

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:28.630
The speech will last for thirty minutes from 11:30 to 12:00.

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:31.420
He needs to get here by then, or he's disqualified!

00:07:31.420 --> 00:07:33.300
What about that made-up article?

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:38.560
Yuu-kun's ratings are dropping, and his supporters are turning to Tatsumi Moheiji.

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:41.060
If this keeps up, he'll lose the election!

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:43.320
I'm so sorry.

00:07:44.510 --> 00:07:46.840
You're... Shiohama-san?

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:48.750
Why are you dressed like a girl?

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:51.990
It turns out our executives had connections with the General Affairs Commission!

00:07:54.010 --> 00:07:57.380
They told me to wear both boys' and girls' uniforms on different occasions

00:07:57.380 --> 00:08:00.120
so that I could collect news anywhere.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:06.130
But in reality, the records had me down as two people, a boy and a girl!

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:09.300
They inflated the number of club members?

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:12.340
They were able to request more club funds this way.

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:14.240
And they made a deal with the General Affairs Commission

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:17.680
to help them in emergencies,
provided that they overlook it.

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:20.890
So the General Affairs Commission made them publish that report?

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:23.560
If Oojima-senpai never shows up...

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:27.180
...people will assume he ran away in fear of being questioned,

00:08:27.180 --> 00:08:29.070
and he'll definitely lose.

00:08:33.270 --> 00:08:34.280
What the heck—

00:08:36.610 --> 00:08:37.530
Hello?

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:41.480
Next, come to Yotsuba Bridge by 11:30.

00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:44.500
You're part of the Katahira Faction, aren't you?

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:48.360
Stopping the President from supporting my campaign wasn't enough,

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:50.800
so you decided to sabotage me directly.

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:52.760
Don't stick your nose where it doesn't belong.

00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:56.470
Damn it!

00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:00.180
Huh? Oojima-kun!

00:09:00.530 --> 00:09:02.240
What happened to you?

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:03.180
You're a mess!

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:05.200
Did you get into a fight or something?

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:06.940
It's nothing.

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:09.800
Oojima-kun, isn't today Election Day?

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:12.700
Yeah, should you even be here right now?

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:13.980
It's okay.

00:09:13.980 --> 00:09:14.950
See you.

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:18.540
He doesn't look "okay" at all.

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:24.370
Ladies and gentlemen, now is the time for a true reform!

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:25.570
And there's only one candidate who can make that happen!

00:09:25.570 --> 00:09:26.940
Oojima-kun...

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:29.020
And there's only one candidate who can make that happen!

00:09:31.290 --> 00:09:32.960
Oh, Matsuri-chan?

00:09:32.970 --> 00:09:34.920
What? Oojima-kun is...

00:09:37.350 --> 00:09:40.930
This is bad! Yuu-kun was seen near Asaoka Academy!

00:09:42.110 --> 00:09:43.700
Satsuki just texted me.

00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:47.310
Her friend saw Yuu-kun alone with his clothes all torn up.

00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:50.260
Oojima-kun and Sumiyoshi-san are missing,

00:09:50.260 --> 00:09:53.280
but the two aren't together.

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:56.500
Furthermore, Oojima-kun seems to have run into trouble.

00:09:56.500 --> 00:09:57.740
Do you think...

00:09:57.740 --> 00:10:00.200
Someone must be obstructing him from attending the election.

00:10:00.650 --> 00:10:01.940
This is an emergency.

00:10:01.940 --> 00:10:03.600
Please locate those two.

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:04.500
Yes, sir!

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:07.760
Their cell phones are turned off!

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:10.130
You won't be able to track them down with GPS!

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:11.580
That's not a problem.

00:10:11.580 --> 00:10:15.670
We prepared for cases like this by taking the liberty of installing transmitters on all Food Club members.

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:17.340
Seriously?!

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:19.850
Excuse me.

00:10:20.630 --> 00:10:21.720
It's me.

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:23.010
Do you have my smartphone?

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:24.520
Your smartphone, Kana?

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:26.540
Check what's inside.

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:30.060
The passcode is 3216, and...

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:34.900
Oosawa Yuina, pattern black. Be careful.

00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:38.040
Summon the intelligence team immediately!

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:38.950
Yes, sir!

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:54.420
Thank you for your time.

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:56.380
Next we have a speech from Oojima Yuuki, an independent candidate.

00:10:56.380 --> 00:10:59.840
Oojima Yuuki

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:02.400
However, he has yet to arrive.

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:04.820
Please wait patiently just a little longer.

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:15.280
The next one will be the last.

00:11:15.280 --> 00:11:18.660
I'll tell you where the girl is once we confirm you're there.

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:19.650
All right.

00:11:20.170 --> 00:11:25.000
You couldn't give your election speech today for the following reason:

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:27.700
You ran away because you were afraid.

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.480
Tell that to everyone.

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:34.220
So that the election isn't declared null and void due to the incident?

00:11:35.910 --> 00:11:37.820
I knew it.

00:11:37.820 --> 00:11:39.860
I'm sure you get it by now.

00:11:39.860 --> 00:11:42.260
This is how an election works.

00:11:43.450 --> 00:11:45.780
Make sure the girl keeps her mouth shut about this.

00:11:45.780 --> 00:11:50.420
If you defy my orders, more people around you will be hurt.

00:11:50.420 --> 00:11:51.440
Are we clear?

00:11:52.570 --> 00:11:54.240
Now this is the last one.

00:11:54.240 --> 00:11:56.040
The location is to the south of Ginjichou Station—

00:11:58.410 --> 00:12:00.380
Oojima-kun, do you hear me?

00:12:00.380 --> 00:12:01.400
That voice...

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:02.240
President Mouri?!

00:12:02.690 --> 00:12:06.020
Sumiyoshi-san is being held in the storage vault of the Lock Gate.

00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:06.990
Please hurry.

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:09.640
I'm on it. Thank you, President!

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:12.100
Are we clear?

00:12:12.100 --> 00:12:16.090
Hey, are you listening, Oojima Yuuki?

00:12:17.030 --> 00:12:19.500
I jacked your line.

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:25.060
This is Oogibashi Kana's smartphone.

00:12:25.060 --> 00:12:28.220
She called me earlier and asked me to check the data in it.

00:12:28.730 --> 00:12:35.230
The images taken by the camera that night were set to transfer here automatically.

00:12:35.670 --> 00:12:39.880
We found pictures of a Public Safety Commission member in the Katahira Faction

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:42.880
and a General Affairs Commission officer engaging in a backroom deal.

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:47.540
And last, but not least, we found a picture taken with this smartphone

00:12:47.540 --> 00:12:51.250
that shows the car that hit Kana as it left the scene.

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:58.250
You're the one who hit Kana.

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:04.340
Public Safety Commissioner Oosawa Yuina,

00:13:04.340 --> 00:13:06.460
I hereby place you under arrest.

00:13:09.250 --> 00:13:11.700
It's all your fault, Yakumo-senpai.

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:14.440
You didn't listen to Katahira-senpai.

00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:15.810
What do you mean?

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:20.440
So long as they're obedient, it doesn't have to be someone from the Public Safety Commission.

00:13:20.870 --> 00:13:22.720
So you were dealing with them all along.

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:24.740
The campus was kept safe the entire time, wasn't it?

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:26.240
And the financial aid discrimination?

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:32.240
Oh, with that minority facing discrimination, there wasn't any conflict among the other students.

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:34.820
It's what every nation does.

00:13:34.820 --> 00:13:37.420
You're too much of a perfectionist.

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:41.090
It truly is my fault for appointing you.

00:13:41.610 --> 00:13:44.760
At this point, Oojima Yuuki has no chance of being elected.

00:13:45.250 --> 00:13:49.920
If the General Affairs Commission wins the election, the Katahira Faction will stay in power.

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:54.020
And of course, everything will remain the same.

00:14:08.930 --> 00:14:10.820
Chisato! Chisato!

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:14.080
Chisato!

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:15.250
Yuuki?

00:14:16.430 --> 00:14:19.020
What happened to the election?

00:14:19.020 --> 00:14:20.000
I skipped it.

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:20.960
Huh?

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:24.110
You're more important to me.

00:14:24.110 --> 00:14:27.680
You're more important to me than anything else.

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:32.190
You're safe... I'm so happy...

00:14:32.190 --> 00:14:33.820
Yuuki...

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:36.820
Well, I'm not!

00:14:37.970 --> 00:14:39.020
What are you doing?!

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:41.100
I should be asking you that!

00:14:41.100 --> 00:14:42.840
Do you hear yourself right now?

00:14:42.840 --> 00:14:44.780
But... I came here for you...

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:47.650
You belong to more than just yourself right now.

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:49.780
You belong to more than just me, too!

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:53.120
You're shouldering everyone's hope.

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:56.080
Do you plan on throwing
away everyone's hard work?

00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:57.620
Chisato...

00:14:57.620 --> 00:14:58.940
But it's too late.

00:14:58.940 --> 00:15:01.080
Not so fast!

00:15:01.570 --> 00:15:03.520
It's too late to give up!

00:15:03.520 --> 00:15:04.840
You have to believe in yourself!

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:07.760
How did you two get up here?!

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:10.060
Don't concern yourself with that.

00:15:10.060 --> 00:15:11.640
Just get on, you two!

00:15:12.610 --> 00:15:13.550
Yeah!

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:18.000
Where do you think you're touching me?!

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:19.390
What else am I supposed to hold on to?!

00:15:19.390 --> 00:15:21.850
We just got a call saying that he's coming!

00:15:21.850 --> 00:15:24.020
Please wait just a little longer!

00:15:24.020 --> 00:15:26.720
But he doesn't have that much time lef—

00:15:26.720 --> 00:15:28.280
Sorry for being late!

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:29.660
Yuu-kun!

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:33.320
All right!

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:34.530
Thank you for your patience.

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:38.040
Oojima Yuuki, an independent candidate, will now give his speech.

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:41.640
I apologize for my tardiness.

00:15:41.640 --> 00:15:43.280
I'm Oojima Yuuki.

00:15:43.280 --> 00:15:44.920
Everyone, I—

00:15:46.370 --> 00:15:48.300
Your speech time has expired.

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:51.620
This completes the speeches for all candidates.

00:15:51.620 --> 00:15:56.500
Students, please cast your ballots into the box by the exit of the auditorium

00:15:56.500 --> 00:15:58.380
before you return to your classrooms.

00:15:58.380 --> 00:15:59.930
I repeat...

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:01.270
Everyone!

00:16:03.950 --> 00:16:05.940
I'm going to talk to myself.

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:07.420
You're out of time!

00:16:07.420 --> 00:16:09.500
You don't have to listen,

00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:12.400
but there's something I've got to say, so...

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:14.320
You have to leave the stage. It's over now!

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:16.460
Please give me just a little bit of time!

00:16:16.460 --> 00:16:18.680
No! You'll be disqualified!

00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:19.720
Please wait.

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:23.250
Let me talk to myself for a moment, too.

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:24.750
Shinonome-san!

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:28.580
An election is an important event that decides the future of the school.

00:16:28.580 --> 00:16:31.600
As a member of the Student Council and a student myself,

00:16:31.600 --> 00:16:36.140
I'd regret seeing a potential topic for debate left out due to a time constraint.

00:16:36.590 --> 00:16:38.980
Don't you feel the same way, Mr. Tatsumi?

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:43.140
Oh, yes, I agree wholeheartedly!

00:16:43.140 --> 00:16:46.400
Please support your open-minded candidate, Tatsumi Moheiji!

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:48.040
But...

00:16:51.170 --> 00:16:52.260
Hello?

00:16:52.260 --> 00:16:53.400
President Mouri?!

00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:55.460
You have my permission.

00:16:55.460 --> 00:16:56.660
Give him time.

00:17:02.250 --> 00:17:05.160
All right, tell them everything that happened!

00:17:05.160 --> 00:17:07.000
Let's rack up those sympathy votes!

00:17:09.610 --> 00:17:15.000
I... I must first apologize to all of you.

00:17:15.570 --> 00:17:16.390
I...

00:17:16.810 --> 00:17:19.140
was in a partnership with President Mouri of the Public Safety Commission!

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:20.240
Huh?

00:17:21.190 --> 00:17:22.640
That's not what we meant!

00:17:23.070 --> 00:17:28.150
I was only able to successfully garner support thanks to his expertise.

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:32.650
I only figured out how an election worked after I entered the race.

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:35.400
I learned what it takes to win an election.

00:17:36.170 --> 00:17:39.520
Raising campaign funds, creating a positive image for myself,

00:17:39.520 --> 00:17:42.140
using political strategies, making connections with the right people,

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:44.910
coming up with promising slogans to win over the voters...

00:17:45.390 --> 00:17:48.940
Not once did I hear the word "justice."

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:52.640
I tried to include a statement on financial aid student harassment in my manifesto,

00:17:52.640 --> 00:17:53.670
but I was opposed.

00:17:54.290 --> 00:17:56.580
It was more important to prey upon

00:17:56.580 --> 00:17:59.930
the weaknesses of my rivals than to develop my own policies.

00:18:00.430 --> 00:18:03.060
People told me that the most important thing in an election is to win,

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:05.860
and that I can do the right thing after I got elected.

00:18:05.860 --> 00:18:08.030
And they're exactly right.

00:18:08.030 --> 00:18:11.190
But... But something feels wrong.

00:18:11.790 --> 00:18:15.360
You can say that I'm being too immature.

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:18.440
I know that ideals aren't always feasible.

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:22.600
But I really don't think I can do my job well

00:18:22.600 --> 00:18:25.720
when I've been elected with votes I won through lies.

00:18:25.720 --> 00:18:29.210
So I want to tell you the truth.

00:18:29.870 --> 00:18:35.220
I initially ran for president to prevent the Food Club from being disbanded.

00:18:35.710 --> 00:18:39.970
It was all for the sake of a club where we just eat snacks and chat every day.

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:44.120
I began my election campaign for that ridiculous reason,

00:18:44.120 --> 00:18:48.340
but I experienced many things in the process,

00:18:48.340 --> 00:18:52.200
and there's one thing I've come to realize.

00:18:52.200 --> 00:18:53.160
And that's...

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:57.740
And that's the fact that I love all of you!

00:18:58.860 --> 00:19:01.570
The Food Club members, the people helping me run my campaign,

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:05.080
those of you who support me, and even the rivals who oppose me.

00:19:05.390 --> 00:19:08.580
That's how I feel, whether you're with me or against me.

00:19:08.970 --> 00:19:11.330
I love this school and all of its students!

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:15.460
It's because I love you all so much that I hate seeing you fighting amongst yourselves!

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:21.220
So, to stop all those conflicts, to see everyone join hands, I decided to hang in there and win.

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:25.930
And I believe all of you can make that happen.

00:19:26.360 --> 00:19:31.960
I can tell from how you're all listening to me talk to myself without leaving!

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:39.120
Even if I don't win this election, I'm glad I could get my message out to all of you.

00:19:39.120 --> 00:19:41.240
That's enough for me.

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:44.450
Thank you for listening, everyone.

00:20:17.430 --> 00:20:19.990
Having a drink while watching the leaves change colors is one of life's great luxuries.

00:20:19.990 --> 00:20:24.140
It's even more fun to watch this change color!

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:27.440
What flavor is that?

00:20:27.990 --> 00:20:30.340
Is this leftovers-on-rice flavor?

00:20:30.340 --> 00:20:31.720
Spot on!

00:20:31.720 --> 00:20:33.250
How do you like the taste?

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:34.460
Normal...

00:20:35.110 --> 00:20:36.420
Actually, tastier.

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:37.590
Seriously?!

00:20:38.550 --> 00:20:41.530
It really took me by surprise.

00:20:41.530 --> 00:20:42.590
Oh, really?

00:20:42.950 --> 00:20:47.830
He didn't make appealing campaign promises, nor did he attack other candidates.

00:20:47.830 --> 00:20:51.100
It was a very unusual approach to an election campaign.

00:20:51.100 --> 00:20:54.730
But he earned the voters' trust that he'd do his job.

00:20:54.730 --> 00:20:56.100
Isn't that all he needs?

00:20:56.100 --> 00:20:57.560
You're right.

00:20:57.560 --> 00:21:00.030
But things will only get more difficult from here on out.

00:21:00.030 --> 00:21:01.110
Excuse me.

00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:03.650
Oh, welcome, our new club member!

00:21:04.050 --> 00:21:07.820
We just started taste-testing a new Yaoi Stick flavor.

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:11.020
Sorry, but I don't have time for that right now.

00:21:11.020 --> 00:21:15.340
I'm so busy fixing the holes in the President's sloppy policies.

00:21:15.340 --> 00:21:17.420
I'm sure being Vice President is a lot of work.

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:20.320
So where is President Oojima?

00:21:20.320 --> 00:21:23.100
Today is a special day for those two.

00:21:23.100 --> 00:21:24.140
A special day?

00:21:33.610 --> 00:21:35.660
Did you get to talk to Daiki-kun?

00:21:35.660 --> 00:21:36.350
Yeah. I told him everything.

00:21:36.350 --> 00:21:38.220
Sumiyoshi Family Grave
Yeah. I told him everything.

00:21:38.220 --> 00:21:39.880
Yeah. I told him everything.

00:21:39.880 --> 00:21:43.840
Me, too. I told him everything.

00:21:58.530 --> 00:21:59.290
Yuuki.

00:21:59.290 --> 00:22:00.220
Hm?

00:22:06.190 --> 00:22:08.940
This chocolate is delicious.

00:22:09.770 --> 00:22:10.540
Yeah.

00:22:20.310 --> 00:22:24.580
In the classroom, looking out the window,
kyoushitsu no madobe de nagameru

00:22:24.580 --> 00:22:29.070
Watching the sky fade softly into twilight,
yasashii yuugure no sora

00:22:29.070 --> 00:22:32.600
I turn around, and there you are again
furimukeba kimi ga egao de

00:22:32.600 --> 00:22:37.290
Looking at me, you smile
kocchi wo miteta

00:22:37.290 --> 00:22:41.000
"Let's go home," you always say,
issho ni kaerou itsumo no

00:22:41.000 --> 00:22:45.790
Going all the places we go every day
toomawari wo shinagara

00:22:45.790 --> 00:22:49.100
Your fingers are just a step away
mada sukoshi todokanai

00:22:49.100 --> 00:22:56.300
But deep inside me, it hurts not holding your hand
yubisaki ga tada setsunakute

00:22:57.930 --> 00:23:02.360
In my heart, I found all these hopes and dreams
ano hi kimi to meguriaeta kara

00:23:02.360 --> 00:23:06.580
Because on that day we happened to meet
takusan no yume wo mitsuketan da

00:23:06.580 --> 00:23:08.740
Even when I wanted to cry,
nakitai toki demo

00:23:08.740 --> 00:23:12.420
You always stayed right there by my side
itsumo soba ni ite kurete

00:23:12.420 --> 00:23:15.530
I want to thank you so much
doumo arigatou

00:23:15.530 --> 00:23:19.260
What I wrote on that page I hid from you
no-to ni kaita himitsu no pe-ji wa

00:23:19.260 --> 00:23:23.140
Were the words that I just couldn't say
zutto iezu ni ita kotoba

00:23:23.140 --> 00:23:28.900
Now they float forever as whispers on the wind
ima kaze no naka zutto sasayaku yo nee

00:23:28.900 --> 00:23:37.300
Listen close, it says, "I love you so much"
kiite kimi ga daisuki da yo

00:23:43.260 --> 00:23:46.570
Don't you think making sweets at home could be a lot of fun?

00:23:46.570 --> 00:23:48.360
Yeah, fun for <i>you</i>, maybe!

00:23:48.360 --> 00:23:50.330
You don't know what it feels like to be your victim!

00:23:50.330 --> 00:23:54.240
Don't be mean! You make it sound like my cooking is inedible.

00:23:54.240 --> 00:23:56.170
"Sound like"? That's <i>exactly</i> what I'm saying!

00:23:56.170 --> 00:24:00.620
Guess what! I brought some homemade chocolate as a surprise treat, Yuuki.

00:24:00.620 --> 00:24:01.440
Have a taste.

00:24:01.440 --> 00:24:02.560
Seriously?

00:24:02.560 --> 00:24:05.770
Next time, Episode 13: "Crossover!"

00:24:05.770 --> 00:24:10.430
How did you make it taste so terrible just by melting and shaping the chocolate?
